[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-CANON
TITLE: The canon
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: callout
TAGS: whole canon, not settled
STATEMENT: >>>
This page is the canon: every node of the committed, human-reviewed contents, rendered from one export. The systems table beneath is the switches. Each row names the part of the repository a body of nodes documents, by the directories that hold it; a node shows when any system holding it is on, and an edge when both its ends show ([LINK: DEC-SYSTEM-IS-A-SOURCE-SET]). The model is always on, because every other system cites it. Switching changes what is shown and never what was rendered, and the selection rides in the page's address so a link carries it.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-SYSTEM-IS-A-TYPE-SET:0000000
NAR-TERM-CANON:0000000
<<<
